@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Explicit carrier propulsion scope — source candidate
+
+Against consolidated PR12 `2212bd81f205e4af3d7f4ff0a1920a6450a46c4f`.
+This preserves Basil's newer main console and bounded Duna panel. It replaces
+only DunaMissionPlanner.cs and adds two Duna source files, tests and this guide.
+No plugin is installed, hardware is changed, or mission is executed.
+
+The previous estimator rejected every attached mixed-propellant engine, so a
+carrier with a shut-down stowed lander could not be previewed. The new preview
+requires explicit selection of the PRIMARY engine parts and fuel tanks. Nothing
+is auto-selected from part names, construction IDs, stage numbers or role labels.
+Actual runtime flightIDs are bound to the current Game/save/vessel/part set.
+
+## Future disposable QA procedure
+
+Do not run during either human's active-play hold. After those holds are released,
+use a freshly prepared separate profile and record exact source/DLL/game/mod
+identities. Native UI, capture and flow qualification remain required.
+
+1. Load the new full-fleet commissioning fixture through normal KSP startup and
+   scenario initialization. Observe the actual clone prefabs, ship mass,
+   requested payload flow locks, all engines off and no active campaign.
+2. Open DUNA EXPEDITION (Control–Option–D on macOS). Choose primary propulsion.
+   Inspect the live part identities; select the four carrier LV-N parts.
+3. Select the three main LF tanks AND the two fuel-bearing Mk3 adapters. Inspect
+   actual amounts/locks rather than using this list as proof. Leave lander tanks
+   excluded and locked. Recovery MonoPropellant and other payload resources are
+   not transfer fuel. Selection changes no KSP object, engine, stage or lock.
+4. Search. Check the nominal wet/retained mass, 15% selected-fuel reserve,
+   primary thrust/Isp and actual selected tank totals against independent stock
+   observations. The hardware candidate's nominal reference is 32,250 primary
+   LF units / 240 kN / 800 s, with lander LF held inside retained mass.
+5. Exercise refusal: unselected matching fuel unlocked, selected tank locked,
+   wrong fuel tank, missing engine/tank, selected multimode/mixed engine,
+   selected nonrestartable/fixed-throttle engine, any attached engine ignited.
+   Do not accept a false result alone without establishing the intended context.
+6. Confirm changing any selected resource amount, engine settings, vessel mass,
+   locks, part membership, Game/save/vessel or body invalidates the itinerary.
+   Pause/warp invalidates completed results too. Starting a campaign makes this
+   pre-start itinerary unavailable. Test game reload with new flightIDs; no old
+   selection is persisted or automatically rebound.
+7. Check every selection row, scrolling, search/cancel/close and GUI input lock.
+   Requests that change the scroll tree are deferred to Update, rather than
+   rebuilding it halfway through a mouse event. This is an implementation choice,
+   not observed proof that the menu works at a particular display/UI scale.
+
+## Read-only capture/model contract
+
+Snapshots copy immutable part, engine and resource observations. Capture reads
+actual KSP mass, engine propellant metadata, vacuum curve, max thrust, limiter,
+ignition/restart/shutdown/throttle flags, and resource density/amount/flowState.
+No stock setters, activation/events, transfer or resource calls occur.
+
+Selected engines must be single-mode, single-propellant, restartable,
+shutdown-capable and throttleable, with equal vacuum Isp. All attached engines,
+including excluded payload engines, must be shut down when planning. Excluded
+shut-down mixed engines no longer poison the carrier's explicit scope. Every
+unselected tank containing a positive amount of matching fuel must be locked;
+empty unlocked tanks do not add imaginary fuel. Density/amount, ratio, mass,
+identity and ambiguous-module errors refuse rather than guess.
+
+Only selected, unlocked primary fuel is spendable by the nominal model. 15%
+remains reserved; every other resource and payload remains in retained mass.
+A canonical signature covers part membership, engine observations, selected
+identities, matching fuel inventory/locks and total wet mass. The adapter
+rechecks around twice per real second and cancels stale searches/results.
+Zero-mass EC amount changes alone do not invalidate a fuel snapshot.
+
+## Evidence and limits
+
+- 71 pure-model assertions pass, including the nominal 127-part fleet budget,
+  locked payload exclusion, explicit selection, unsupported/ignited engine and
+  inventory refusals, snapshot immutability, ordering and freshness signatures.
+- 29 assertions compile the actual production capture against recording,
+  read-only KSP boundary doubles. They cover real fields used, units/limiter,
+  unchanged source state, locks, missing metadata and unsupported contexts.
+- Full 42-source KSP1.12.5 build passes. Existing 608 Duna route-model assertions
+  pass unchanged. No native KSP run follows from these results.
+
+This is still an impulsive/nominal input estimator. It does NOT prove stock
+crossfeed connectivity, stage/thermal/ignition dynamics, actual tank draw,
+finite burns or trajectories. No maneuver nodes, throttle, resource locks,
+crew, saves, universe time or warp are written. Selecting an engine is not
+Hamish/Basil burn approval. Landed/ascent/recovery vehicles need their own
+qualified models; the conservative Ares ~86 m/s deficit is unchanged. Native
+GUI, planet ephemerides, docking state, payload separation, actual freeze/thaw,
+background power, accelerated watches and the full mission remain unqualified.
